# Split BLE bond recovery options. Provides two complementary self-healing
# paths so a desync between the dongle (central) and a Hillside View half
# (peripheral) can recover without reflashing:
#
#   1. DONGLE_BOND_AUTOHEAL - automatic on the dongle, reacts to BLE
#      security failures (bond/encryption desync).
#
#   2. PERIPHERAL_BOOT_BONDCLEAR - user-triggered on a half, reacts to a
#      key combo held at boot. Covers the case where the BLE link is up
#      but no input flows (GATT/CCC desync), which the dongle hook
#      cannot detect on its own.

menu "Dongle / split BLE bond recovery"

config DONGLE_BOND_AUTOHEAL
    bool "Dongle: auto-clear stale split bonds on BLE security failure"
    depends on BT && BT_SMP && ZMK_SPLIT && ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    help
      When the dongle (central) connects to a split peripheral and
      BLE encryption / authentication fails - typically because of a
      stale or corrupted bond on either side - automatically unpair
      that peripheral. The next connection attempt will then do a
      fresh just-works pairing instead of refusing the link.

      Pair this with CONFIG_BT_SMP_ALLOW_UNAUTH_OVERWRITE=y on the
      peripherals so they accept the dongle's new keys to overwrite
      their own stale bond. With both ends configured the link
      self-heals from a bond desync without any reflash or
      settings_reset UF2.

      Successful connections (the normal sleep/wake cycle on a
      battery half) are not affected - they fire
      security_changed(SUCCESS) which is ignored. Incoming host
      connections (e.g. HID over BLE) are also ignored; only
      outgoing central-role connections (split peripherals) are
      acted on.

if DONGLE_BOND_AUTOHEAL

config DONGLE_BOND_AUTOHEAL_COOLDOWN_MS
    int "Per-peer cooldown between unpair attempts (ms)"
    default 30000
    help
      Minimum time, in milliseconds, between unpair attempts for
      the same peer address. Prevents pathological loops if pairing
      keeps failing for an unrelated reason.

module = DONGLE_BOND_AUTOHEAL
module-str = dongle_bond_autoheal
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # DONGLE_BOND_AUTOHEAL


config PERIPHERAL_BOOT_BONDCLEAR
    bool "Peripheral: clear bonds at boot when a key combo is held"
    depends on BT && ZMK_SPLIT && !ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    help
      On a split peripheral, watch for a specific key combo during a
      short window after boot. If the combo is held, unpair all
      bonds (including the bond with the central). On the next
      reconnect the peripheral has no stored bond, so SMP does a
      fresh just-works pairing - which clears any stale CCC / GATT
      state on the central side too.

      This is the manual escape hatch for the "BLE link up but no
      input" failure mode that the dongle-side auto-heal cannot
      detect (because security_changed fires with SUCCESS and the
      desync is at the GATT layer above).

      Recovery procedure for the user:
        1. Flip the half's power switch OFF.
        2. Hold the two designated trigger keys.
        3. Flip the power switch back ON, keep holding for ~2 s.
        4. Release. The half re-pairs on its next connection.

      The trigger fires only inside the early boot window, so it
      never interferes with normal typing or with peripheral
      sleep/wake cycles (sleep is not a power cycle - the boot
      window only opens on cold boot).

if PERIPHERAL_BOOT_BONDCLEAR

config PERIPHERAL_BOOT_BONDCLEAR_WINDOW_MS
    int "Boot window during which the trigger combo is sampled (ms)"
    default 2500
    help
      How long after boot the trigger combo is watched for. After
      this window the listener disarms and key events are processed
      normally.

config PERIPHERAL_BOOT_BONDCLEAR_POS_A
    int "First trigger position (half-local matrix position)"
    default 0
    help
      Half-local matrix position number for the first key of the
      trigger combo. Position 0 is the top-outermost key of the
      half (top-left of the left half, top-right of the right half,
      because the matrix is mirrored).

config PERIPHERAL_BOOT_BONDCLEAR_POS_B
    int "Second trigger position (half-local matrix position)"
    default 5
    help
      Half-local matrix position number for the second key of the
      trigger combo. Position 5 is the top-innermost key of the
      half. Both keys must be pressed simultaneously inside the
      boot window for the unpair to fire.

module = PERIPHERAL_BOOT_BONDCLEAR
module-str = peripheral_boot_bondclear
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # PERIPHERAL_BOOT_BONDCLEAR

endmenu
